        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Registered File no. 9901/1926.\n\nHistorical significance: \"According to Hadjimichaeli (p. 14), dark red dresses with silk embroidery were worn by married women on feast days--bright red with gold embroidery were for brides and newly-married women\"--Register."@en ;
